abstract: >-
  Difference-side arithmetic of the 3x3 magic square of squares problem:
  a seven-line normal form (three same-difference square progressions on a
  transversal frame) with its integral Smith form; three explicit mechanisms
  producing infinite (8,7) near-miss families with a complete least-shift
  law and a positive-density elliptic-orbit lift; the interaction
  surface for the eighth line, its saturation and full S5 cone monodromy;
  imported fixed-difference finiteness with one completely closed fibre
  and a finite-Kummer-class stop; a five-term S-unit support law with an
  exact mod-8 endpoint/interior table; an Aebi-derived uniqueness result
  for differences with at most three prime factors; and a complete S-unit
  catalogue excluding full magic for differences supported on primes at most
  19, with 384 primitive nine-square/seven-line classes and a sharp relative
  defect bound. Arbitrary four-prime supports remain open.
  Elementary and symbolic computations have exact standard-library Python
  replays. External-CAS ranks, point lists, and Selmer sets enter as
  hash-pinned inputs and normalized output records; the verifier
  authenticates and parses those records but does not independently
  recompute the underlying calculations. Classical ingredients are
  attributed; no priority or firstness is claimed.
